    "result_text": "The build is green with the full suite passing. The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe request: when a create-owner request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, allow an owner at an address already used by a same-last-name owner, assign both the same stable `householdId`, and return it.\n\nMuch of the household infrastructure was already scaffolded (the `DuplicateHousehold`/duplicate-detection path and the `sharesHousehold` request flag). The missing piece was the `householdId` itself. I added it, keeping each concern in its own small unit:\n\n**New logic, placed where it belongs:**\n- **`HouseholdIdGenerator`** (new util) \u2014 sole responsibility: derive a *stable* household id deterministically from the normalized last name + address (SHA-256 \u2192 12 upper-case hex chars). Because it's a pure function of the shared fields, every member of a household derives the same id regardless of creation order, reusing the existing `TextNormalizer` for the case/whitespace canonicalization.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 refactored the existing boolean `sharesHouseholdWithExistingOwner` helper into `findHouseholdMembers` (returns the matching owners rather than just a yes/no), so the same lookup drives both the duplicate-rejection path and the new join path. Added a focused `joinHousehold` helper that assigns the shared id to the new owner and to each existing member (persisting only members whose id actually changes). `createOwner` now returns the `householdId`.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- `Owner` model: new `householdId` field mapped to a `household_id` column.\n- `household_id` column added to all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the script.\n- `openapi.yml`: added the read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema; the generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct mapper pick it up automatically, so it's returned by `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` with no controller change.\n\n**Tests:** the full suite (the `AcceptanceTest`, which creates two owners joining an existing household and asserts they share a non-blank `householdId`) passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures.",
